  "theorem": "For every invertible linear carrier map T and pulled-back potential V'=V o T^{-1}, multilinear chain rule gives D^n V'_{Tx}[Tv,...,Tv]=D^n V_x[v,...,v]. Hence I12 is natural under carrier isomorphisms. Independently, v->c v multiplies numerator and denominator by c^12, so the ratio is projective in the transported direction. This is a carrier-transport theorem, not merely scalar-coordinate invariance."
